# Claude lanes (drive.sh GLM_BACKEND=claude, bakeoff/claude_jail.sh) hold a read-only copy of the subscription OAuth
# credentials, which the model's own tools can read. So their netns reaches only Anthropic's published range
# 160.79.104.0/23 on 443 (api.anthropic.com, platform.claude.com, claude.ai all resolve there): a lane that reads the
# token has nowhere to send it but Anthropic. No DNS either: pasta's forwarder recurses, so query names would be an
# exfiltration channel; the jail gets a pinned /etc/hosts from anthropic_hosts.sh instead. Everything else, IPv6
# included, is rejected.
table inet sbx {
  chain out { type filter hook output priority 0; policy drop;
    ip daddr 160.79.104.0/23 tcp dport 443 accept
    meta l4proto tcp reject with tcp reset
    reject
  }
}
